      en: "The tower of the Church of La Compañía de Jesús in Sucre is a city landmark. The church was built by Jesuits in the 17th century, but the bell tower was completed only in the 19th century. Standing 30 meters tall, it offers panoramic views of Sucre's historic center. The architecture blends Baroque and Neoclassical styles. Inside the church, there is a gilded altar and paintings from the Cusco School. The tower underwent restoration in 2005. Sucre is a UNESCO World Heritage site, and this tower is one of its iconic features.",
